### 2. Passwords Stored in Plaintext
**File:** [`vim_controller.py:56`](file:///d:/SPAR-NSR/AI%20Team/demo_280826/Vendor_Invoice_Management_POC/vim/vim_controller.py#L56), [`vim_controller.py:139`](file:///d:/SPAR-NSR/AI%20Team/demo_280826/Vendor_Invoice_Management_POC/vim/vim_controller.py#L139)

```python
# Login: plaintext comparison
if this_user.PasswordHash == password:  # no hashing!

# Add user: plaintext storage
PasswordHash=request.form['password'],  # stored as-is
```

**Impact:** A critical security vulnerability. Any database leak exposes all user passwords. The field is even called `PasswordHash` yet stores raw text.

**Fix:** Use `werkzeug.security.generate_password_hash` / `check_password_hash`.

