### 3. `admin_required` Does Not Check `login_required` First
**File:** [`vim_controller.py:23-30`](file:///d:/SPAR-NSR/AI%20Team/demo_280826/Vendor_Invoice_Management_POC/vim/vim_controller.py#L23)

```python
def admin_required(view):
    @wraps(view)
    def wrapped(*args, **kwargs):
        if session.get('role') != 'admin':
            flash("Admin access required.", "danger")
            return redirect(url_for('login'))   # ← no login check
        return view(*args, **kwargs)
    return wrapped
```

**Impact:** An unauthenticated user with no session gets the confusing "Admin access required" flash instead of being properly redirected as unauthenticated. Also, admin routes are never stacked with `@login_required`, so authentication state is only checked implicitly via `role`.

