### 4. `app` Name Conflict / Stale Global in `app.py`
**File:** [`app.py:13`](file:///d:/SPAR-NSR/AI%20Team/demo_280826/Vendor_Invoice_Management_POC/app.py#L13)

```python
app = None          # global set to None
...
def create_app():
    app = Flask(__name__)  # local variable shadows the global
    ...
    return app

app = create_app()  # overwrites global — works by accident
```

**Impact:** The `app = None` at module level and the re-assignment inside `create_app()` creates a local variable (not the global). This works *only* because `app = create_app()` then assigns at module level. But any code that tries to reference the global `app` before `create_app()` returns will see `None`. Also `app.debug = True` is set inside the factory but `app.run(debug=True)` is also set — debug mode is doubly enabled which is a security risk in any deployment.

