### 6. `admin_toggle_user` and `admin_delete_user` Use GET for State-Changing Operations
**File:** [`vim_controller.py:168`](file:///d:/SPAR-NSR/AI%20Team/demo_280826/Vendor_Invoice_Management_POC/vim/vim_controller.py#L168), [`vim_controller.py:187`](file:///d:/SPAR-NSR/AI%20Team/demo_280826/Vendor_Invoice_Management_POC/vim/vim_controller.py#L187)

```python
@app.route('/admin/users/toggle/<int:user_id>')   # GET only
@app.route('/admin/users/delete/<int:user_id>')   # GET only
```

**Impact:** These are state-changing operations exposed over GET. This violates HTTP semantics and is a **CSRF vulnerability** — a malicious link can delete/toggle any user just by getting the admin to visit a URL. Same issue exists for vendor toggle/delete routes.

