### 10. `TaxValidation` Uses Exact Float Equality
**File:** [`stages.py:314`](file:///d:/SPAR-NSR/AI%20Team/demo_280826/Vendor_Invoice_Management_POC/vim/validation_setup/validation/stages.py#L314)

```python
if calculated_total != actual_total:   # exact float comparison
```

**Impact:** Although `round(..., 2)` is applied, floating-point arithmetic can still produce values like `100.00000000001` vs `100.0`. This can cause false-positive validation failures on perfectly valid invoices, especially when line items are summed.

**Fix:** Use `abs(calculated_total - actual_total) > 0.01` tolerance check.

