## 🟡 Medium-Severity Bugs

### 12. Unused Import in `vim_controller.py`
**File:** [`vim_controller.py:1-4`](file:///d:/SPAR-NSR/AI%20Team/demo_280826/Vendor_Invoice_Management_POC/vim/vim_controller.py#L1)

```python
from importlib.resources import files   # never used
from flask import app, ...              # imports `app` from flask (wrong!)
from yaml import load_all              # never used
```

- `from flask import app` — there is no `app` export from flask; this shadows the local `app` parameter in `register_routes(app)` and could cause `NameError` in certain call paths.
- `load_all` from yaml is never used.
- `files` from `importlib.resources` is never used.

---

### 13. `admin_invoice_extraction` Shadows Built-in `load_all`
**File:** [`vim_controller.py:584`](file:///d:/SPAR-NSR/AI%20Team/demo_280826/Vendor_Invoice_Management_POC/vim/vim_controller.py#L584)

```python
from vim.extraction.json_store import load_all, ENRICHED_PATH
```

This locally imports `load_all` within the route. Meanwhile, `from yaml import load_all` is imported at the top of the file. The local import shadows the top-level one — this works correctly but is confusing and fragile. The yaml `load_all` import at the top is completely dead code.

