### 14. `get_collection()` is Cached with `@lru_cache` but May Become Stale
**File:** [`store.py:30-39`](file:///d:/SPAR-NSR/AI%20Team/demo_280826/Vendor_Invoice_Management_POC/vim/rag/store.py#L30)

```python
@lru_cache(maxsize=1)
def get_collection(name: str = CHROMA_COLLECTION_NAME) -> chromadb.Collection:
```

**Impact:** If `CHROMA_COLLECTION_NAME` changes at runtime or the ChromaDB client needs to be re-initialized, the cached collection object is never refreshed. Also, `lru_cache` is not thread-safe under heavy concurrent Flask requests (though threaded Flask calls with `threaded=True` can hit this).

