### 16. `insert_record` Does Not Flush Before `_upsert_ocr_extraction`
**File:** [`load.py:136-171`](file:///d:/SPAR-NSR/AI%20Team/demo_280826/Vendor_Invoice_Management_POC/vim/extraction/load.py#L136)

```python
if existing_doc:
    invoice = db.session.get(Invoice, existing_doc.InvoiceID)
    ...
    document = existing_doc
else:
    invoice = Invoice(**invoice_fields)
    db.session.add(invoice)
    db.session.flush()        # gets invoice.InvoiceID
    document = InvoiceDocument(...)
    db.session.add(document)
    db.session.flush()        # gets document.DocumentID

_upsert_ocr_extraction(document, record)   # accesses document.ocr_extraction
```

When `existing_doc` is found (update path), `document.ocr_extraction` may be a lazy-loaded relationship that hits the DB — but since the session hasn't been flushed after the `invoice_fields` update, there could be stale relationship data. Minor but can cause subtle bugs on re-uploads.

