### 17. `POMatching` Stage Never Queries the Database
**File:** [`stages.py:240-279`](file:///d:/SPAR-NSR/AI%20Team/demo_280826/Vendor_Invoice_Management_POC/vim/validation_setup/validation/stages.py#L240)

```python
purchase_orders = context.get("purchase_orders", {})
po = purchase_orders.get(po_number)
if not po:
    return { "status": "FAILED", "message": "Purchase order not found" }
```

`run_validation.py` always passes `context={}` — so `purchase_orders` is always an empty dict. This means **every invoice will fail PO Matching**, even if a valid PO exists in the database. The stage should query `PurchaseOrder` from the DB instead of relying on context injection.

